  "description": "AZEWAH crystallizes in the orthorhombic crystal system with space group P 21 21 21. Reported CIF formula moiety: C168 H100 Er4 O16 4-,4(C5 H14 N3 1+),6(C1 H2 Cl2),1.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.692-3.768 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.17-105.51°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C168H100Er4O16·4(C5H14N3)·6(CH2Cl2)·1.5(H2O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
